-- title:
--   Generator of ⋆-alternating forms is a perfect pairing
-- statement:
--   Let $q,q'$ be primes with $q'\neq q$ and let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ be such that the quaternion algebra $B=\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ satisfies `IsIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt`, i.e. $0<a$ or $0<b$, and for every height-one prime $v$ of the ring of integers of $\mathbb{Q}$ the completion $B\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ has all its nonzero elements invertible exactly when $v$ contains $q$ or $q'$. Let $\Lambda\subseteq B$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule which is a maximal order: it contains $1$, is closed under multiplication, spans $B$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, is finitely generated, and any order containing it equals it. Let $\mu\in\Lambda$ satisfy $\mu^{2}=-(qq')\cdot 1$, and let $\mathrm{star}:\Lambda\to\Lambda$ be a function with $\mu\cdot\mathrm{star}(x)=\bar{x}\mu$ for all $x\in\Lambda$, where $\bar{\phantom{x}}$ is quaternion conjugation. Let $R$ be a commutative domain of characteristic zero and $M$ an $R$-module, and let $\rho$ assign to each element of $\Lambda$ an $R$-linear endomorphism of $M$, additively, sending $1$ to the identity and a product $xy$ to $\rho(x)\circ\rho(y)$. Assume $M$ is free of rank one over $\rho(\Lambda)$ on a vector $e$ in the following explicit sense: for some $\mathbb{Z}$-basis $(\,b_\Lambda(i)\,)_{i\in\iota}$ of $\Lambda$ there is an $R$-basis of $M$ indexed by the same $\iota$ whose $i$-th member is $\rho(b_\Lambda(i))e$. Finally let $E_0:M\times M\to R$ be $R$-bilinear with $E_0(m,m)=0$ for all $m$ and $E_0(\rho(x)m,n)=E_0(m,\rho(\mathrm{star}\,x)n)$ for all $x\in\Lambda$ and $m,n\in M$, and assume every bilinear form with these two properties is of the shape $r\cdot E_0$ for some $r\in R$. Then $E_0$ is a perfect pairing.
--
--   This is the duality step underlying the Rosati involution on a fake elliptic curve attached to an indefinite quaternion algebra ramified exactly at two primes: the space of $\star$-alternating forms on a rank-one $\Lambda$-module is generated by the form $\mathrm{trd}(\bar{x}\mu^{-1}y)$, and maximality of $\Lambda$ together with $\mu^{2}=-qq'$ makes that generator unimodular at every prime. It is used in the proof that the relevant kernel is trivial for quaternionic fake elliptic curves in the Čerednik–Drinfeld setting.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_QuaternionAlgebra_IsMaximalOrder_isPerfPair_of_generator_of_alternating_starAdjoint_forms.lean

